   A minimal pair is a counterexample (P, Q) to JC such that B = gcd(v1,1 (P ), v1,1 (Q)).
   An (m, n)-pair is a Jacobian pair (P, Q) with P, Q ∈ L(l) for some l, that satisfies certain
