./xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:106:## 5. Numerical semigroups of one-place curves; realization theorems
./xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:108:Target: numerical semigroups of one-place curves; realization theorems. Bearing on residual AM-numerical types and the horn’s torus-knot group family.
./xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:110:**F23. Almirón–Olivares-Fernández, *Topological representations of free numerical semigroups via iterated torus knots*, arXiv:2412.01613v2, 2025-10-06 (to appear, Res. Math. Sci.).** SHA-256 `d65a2f34d2d4a874ea6191841074d668499ea87cfe52e6b2286375b920b0e5a6`. Associates a family of iterated torus knots in \(S^3\) to a free numerical semigroup; computes \(\pi_1\) of each complement; all knots in the family have the same Alexander polynomial, equal (up to a factor) to the Poincaré series of the semigroup. Consequence: families of iterated torus knots with the Alexander polynomial of an irreducible plane-curve singularity that are **not isotopic** to the associated algebraic knot. **STRUCTURE** for the horn’s “torus-knot-with-relators” group family (CENTRAL-RANK / CUSP-PARITY consume this topology): Alexander polynomials do not separate algebraic from non-algebraic iterated-torus knots of a given free semigroup. **Does not** realize or forbid a polynomial one-place curve of a prescribed \(\delta\)-sequence.
./xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:114:**F25. Orevkov, *On curves of degree 10 with 12 triple points*, arXiv:2601.07809v3, 2026-02-09.** SHA-256 `6cedc659d9cb1bb52380a761f51d7380dcf0a41d5aaef9844c2ee3a5cda56d22`. Constructs an irreducible *rational* degree-10 curve with 12 triple points, and a union of three rational quartics with 19 triples; counterexamples to a Dimca–Harbourne–Sticlaru conjecture; an analytic family degenerating to the dual Hesse arrangement plus a line. **IRRELEVANT** to one-place-at-infinity polynomial curves (these are multi-place projective curves with triples, not AM semigroups).
